\subsection{Sessions per GPU}
Figure~\ref{fig:overflow} is the motivation and Fig.~\ref{fig:savings} the payoff. Across the whole tier-ratio sweep the tiered-to-HBM-only sessions-per-GPU ratio stays between \mChatSessionsGainMin$\times$ and \mChatSessionsGainMax$\times$ for chat (and similarly for the other workloads), tracking the tier's capacity multiple rather than the workload's reuse. Adding an order of magnitude of DRAM and SSD capacity fits an order of magnitude more sessions; a good placement policy adds nothing to this count, and its job is instead to protect the latency at which those sessions are served.

